system "BGN-PCGN:ady-Cyrl:Latn:2012" {

metadata {
  authority_id bgnpcgn
  id 2012
  language iso-639-2:ady
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name Romanization of Adyghe (2012)
  url https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/permanent-committee-on-geographical-names
  creation_date 2012
  confirmation_date 2017-10
  description {
    The BGN/PCGN system for Adyghe is designed for use in romanizing names written in the
    Adyghe Cyrillic alphabet. Adyghe, a language of the north-western Caucasian family, is
    principally spoken in Russia's republic of Adygeya and has been written in a modified
    Cyrillic script since 1938. Also known as West Circassian, Adyghe is notable for its
    rich density of consonant phonemes and corresponding paucity of vowels. Adyghe letters
    are addressed in the romanizations as per their articulation: glottalised consonants
    are marked with an apostrophe, labialized consonants with w, and retroflex consonants
    with an underbar. Phonemes shared with Kabardian are represented as per the
    BGN/PCGN Kabardian Romanization System.
  }

  notes {
    note "У should be romanized as w or u according to context: w should be used word-initially, and u used elsewhere."
    note "The characters Ё, Ъ, Ы and Ь (except as they occur in character combinations addressed elsewhere in the table) appear only in Russian loan words, and are thus romanized in the same style as in the BGN/PCGN Romanization System for Russian."
    note "The palochka is romanized ’ except as it occurs in the combination Ӏу."
    note "An inventory of letter-diacritic combinations, with their Unicode encoding, in addition to the unmodified letters of the basic Roman script is:"
    note "All apostrophes appearing in romanization are U+2019"
    note "Ë (U+00CB)  ë (U+00EB)  Ź (U+0179)  ź (U+017A)  Z͟H (U+005A+0048+035F)  z͟h (U+007A+0068+035F)  H̱ (0048+0031)  ẖ (0068+0031)  Č (U+010C)  č (U+010D)  S͟H (U+0053+0048+035F)  s͟h (U+0073+0068+035F)  Ś (U+015A)  ś (U+015B)  Ä (U+00C4)  ä (U+00E4)"
    note "The source document prints the H̱ inventory codepoint as 0048+0031; the glyph shown is h with the combining macron below (U+0331) and the table column shows the precomposed ẖ (U+1E96). This map outputs ẖ (U+1E96)."
    note "The Romanization columns show only lowercase forms but, when romanizing, uppercase and lowercase Roman letters as appropriate should be used."
  }
}

